            <ArticleTitle>Meralgia paresthetica: an unusual complication of cardiac catheterization via the femoral artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>69-71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Nerve complications following cardiac catheterization via the femoral route are rare. We report a case of meralgia paresthetica, a mononeuropathy affecting the lateral cutaneous nerve of the thigh following uncomplicated cardiac catheterization and percutaneous intervention via this route.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright 2002 Wiley-Liss, Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
